# Gentoo penguin

The gentoo penguin breeds on the Antarctic Peninsula and on the subantarctic
islands, recognisable by the white band across the crown and the orange bill. It
pursues krill, squid and small shoaling prey below the surface, beating its
flippers like wings and turning on a wingtip, and is the fastest of its family
under way. Foraging trips are short and shallow compared with those of its
larger relatives, most descents ending within thirty metres of the surface. The
brood is raised on a circular pile of pebbles, and a stolen pebble is a common
cause of quarrel in a colony. See [[spheniscidae]].
